{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1751-cybergnostic-implants","id":1751,"title":"Cybergnostic Implants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-03T07:34:52-08:00","id":1751,"title":"Cybergnostic Implants","content":"I was challenged to run a Cyberpunk <a href=\"https://plus.google.com/events/csl8hiqbqnvk0mfg1hslg399jks\" target=\"_blank\">Bleeding Edge/Demon: the Descent crossover</a>, and one idea I'm playing around with is &quot;cybergnostic impants.&quot; The general idea is that these implants take the place of traditional cyberware, since man-made prosthetics are still quite limited, and allow extra-human abilities.<br /> <br /> Given what we know about Demon, what sort of limitations do you think these implants might have? Would they require Aetheric Resonance to function?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://darker-days.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Darker Days Radio</a> - The World of Darkness Podcast<br /> <a href=\"http://historylessons.libsyn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Unbuttoned History</a> - A History Podcast with Jokes","edited":{"userid":124,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/124-darker-days-mike","user":"Darker Days Mike","date":".  Clarify 11-03-2013, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/124-darker-days-mike","name":"Darker Days Mike","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T17:50:08-08:00","id":2226,"title":"","content":"Well that depends on how you see them as working.<br /> <br /> If they are the reverse engineering of demonic powers or godmachine made goodies, I'd use the standard plug in rules.<br /> <br /> If however they're demon made infrastructure taking the form of cyberware, they ought to use aether, and so aether batteries would have to be included for human cyborgs. Well unless the demons came up with aetheric conversion engines of some sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T23:40:59-08:00","id":2435,"title":"","content":"I'll get back to you on this once <b>Demon: the Descent</b> is released. My gut instinct is that you could do worse than to use Demonic Form powers as inspiration for creating new Plug-Ins. As StSword says, much of the issue depends on where this cyberware comes from: is it the God-Machine trying to warp humans into machines that it can better control? Or is it demons using their pacts to create soldiers to aid them in their shadow war against the God-Machine? The latter option depends at least in part on what sort of pact mechanics <b>Demon</b> provides \u2014 which is why I need to see the game before I can say more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\